                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Great game with great graphics. Runs on even 10yo hardware. Honestly one of my favorites, but I am always deterred because of the difficulty ramp in the roguelike mechanics mixed with no Steam Cloud save file support. This essentially locks me into a cycle where I have to absolutely be sure I backed up the latest file and folder if I want to move machines or need to format my computer for any reason. I never end up being able to progress very far. Despite this, it is a fantastic game. Very fun, and very pleasing to the eye and ear. The gameplay is neat where some windows move on their own in their fake OS as if the entity is haunting it. I'm really glad it's still on steam, but I hope they come out with their \"small update\" soon they hinted at a while back, adding Steam Cloud functionality to the save files among whatever else they were thinking of.",
